{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Release 0.11.0 reproduction from discovered ticket 9874-b1a9-2ff1-4cd3: all 10 exact acceptance-criterion lines rejected by the first completion-verifier finalizer were passed unchanged to operator_evidence_ac_gaps; every line produced no marker and the aggregate result was []. Plan review therefore supplied no evidence-kind coaching, and the runtime/git/CI/external criteria remained untagged despite concrete receipt URLs, timestamps, commands, commits, and hashes in ticket comments. Normal close then failed exactly as ADR 0043 prescribes for untagged codebase-verifiable criteria. After adding the exact [operator-attested] prefix to those criteria, check-ac passed all 31 criteria, refreshed plan review signed PASS at 364cb2327a, and a normal non-force close signed completion-verifier PASS at that SHA after bounded recovery. This is a deterministic detector/coaching gap: the tagged FAIL-to-PASS experiment confirms the completion validator itself honored the intended evidence contract, while rejecting the suspected recovery instruction-locality defect for this incident."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786091325959729001,"uuid":"62140dd0-ee62-4ce4-8123-6ed7e5b4e199"}